meta {
  name: Get Job Status
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ingest/{{jobId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  jobId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

docs {
  # GET /api/v1/ingest/{job_id}

  Look up an ingestion job by id. Reads straight from the Postgres
  `documents` row written by the upload endpoint; the worker updates
  the row's terminal status when the Temporal workflow finishes.

  ## Path parameter
  - **job_id** — the UUID returned by `POST /api/v1/ingest`.

  ## Headers
  - **X-API-Key** *(required)*.

  ## Response 200
  ```json
  {
    "job_id": "5f1c…",
    "status": "completed",
    "path": "s3://kb-uploads/5f1c…/report.pdf",
    "department": "medical",
    "doc_type": "",
    "error": "",
    "summary": ""
  }
  ```

  ## Status values
  - `pending` — workflow not yet picked up by worker.
  - `processing` — `fetch_source` activity ran; workflow in flight.
  - `completed` — vector + graph indexing both succeeded.
  - `vector_only` — vector indexing succeeded, graph half exhausted
    retries (best-effort downgrade — answers still work, graph just
    isn't enriched for this doc).
  - `failed` — vector indexing failed terminally; `error` column
    carries the message. Re-upload to retry.

  ## Error codes
  - `401` — auth.
  - `404` — unknown job id.
}
